+# Independent full-M3 acceptance
+
+**Accept I/R/O/G/V/C within the approved exact-real tetrahedral scope. No blockers or outstanding conditions.** This is the supplied independent composed-M3 verdict, separate from the scoped M3b verdict.
+
+- Mathematical pin: `e2ea538b8da38c01c098ef28a3ea31030d90c6bb`.
+- Tree: `1cf0e361d9b2a323ac23f6f129d26fb3599ec00b`.
+- Worker handoff: `6284949a428e6a6e12fbe98ad21a5b2a10778cfe`.
+- Scientific/representation approval: `3189a603b3f6af953f0828d6b2e239320fd2cd20`.
+- [Original full report](../M3b/independent-e2ea538/report/Review.md), [original decision record](../M3b/independent-e2ea538/report/Review_Record.json), [payload manifest](../M3b/independent-e2ea538/SHA256SUMS).
+
+The preserved accepted M3a I/R/O/conditional-C assembly composes with the accepted M3b G/V/concrete-C construction. All 117 cumulative bindings (66 M2 plus 51 M3) are accepted, with no deferred M3 part. The immutable downstream pin is recorded in specifications/accepted-M3.json and refers to the mathematical candidate, rather than a later documentation checkpoint.
+
+The result covers outgoing integrated residual boundary balance, orientation/relabeling with transported data, derived concrete metric closure, determinant-volume identities and common-state preservation for compatible supplied boundaries in the approved direct-state edge-aggregated original Roe scheme. It does not select a wall/far-field algorithm, define a time update, prove entropy/update positivity, cover mixed meshes or floating-point execution, or establish SU2 correspondence.
+
+The next decision is a separately reviewed M4 boundary proposal, with its exact variant, physical domain and compatibility requirements. Proposal preparation is the next handoff; M4 Lean implementation requires Andrea's scientific approval after review. Original prior-stage evidence and historical pending fields remain unchanged.
